Z||000000||Tom88gt||01-22-2000||08:39 PM||||Does anyone remember Herb Adams suspension kits?  A few years ago Summit Racing used to carry a few (just a few) Herb Adams suspension kits (shocks, springs & sway bars) for some GM cars.  One of the cars happened to be the Fiero.<P>Herb Adams was a suspension engineer for GM until he started his own company.  I figure who else would know more about Fiero handling than Herb?  <P>Does anyone know if his kits are still available?  Summit doesn't list them in the catalog anymore.  But they do list some Herb Adams products still.  But I get the feeling they are close-out specials.  I tried a web search and came up empty.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Monkeyman||01-23-2000||04:09 AM||||I just did a quick search under "Herb Adams" and this is what I came up with:  "Adams Herb Vse, Inc.<BR>Monterey, CA 93940<BR>831-649-8123<BR>------------------<BR>Business Category:<BR>Automotive Parts & Accessories Stores Retail<P>Maybe someone in the Monterey area could make a local call Monday and see if this is the right Herb Adams?||||reg||1
Z||000002||Tom88gt||01-23-2000||07:32 AM||||I got that too.  But I couldn't find a link to it.  But I'll try the phone on Monday.  It seems to be the closest web hit.||||reg||1
Z||000003||lowCG||01-23-2000||10:21 AM||||I must say that the guy has a pretty good background with GM Testing and Development,but I sampled one of those kits once and it was very stiff,way overkill for any street car(ie.no roll cage).The spring design/wind was same as the stock pitch,just that the spring wire was around 5/8 of an inch.The guy said his car had popped the windshield out after putting in this kit.<BR>Good luck.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||2FAST4U||01-23-2000||01:54 PM||||Herb Adams Vse is the company you guys are looking for. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Tom88gt||01-24-2000||12:41 PM||||LowCG, the guy that lost his windshield, do you have anymore details?  Is it possible he had installed it incorrectly or had it way out of adjustment?  <P>I can't imagine a suspension company releasing a product without some sort of "off road use only" disclaimer if the kit is not suitable for street use.||||reg||1
Z||000006||lowCG||01-24-2000||07:16 PM||||He was an ex-GM service manager who worshipped Zora Duntov,and who has a strong background in automotive build quality,blah,blah...<BR>He purchased the kit under the impression that it would be a high-performance improvement I'm sure,just a bit too stiff for his chassis sans roll cage,however.<BR>I'd approached him one day,noticing the huge tires,and lowered stance,about 8 years ago after going through around 50 shock/spring changes to get what I wanted on my car,and was pretty surprised when I felt how firm the setup was after he told me what it was.<BR>Suspensions need to absorb shock very rapidly in order to be effective,not just react to bumps/surface.<BR>My favorite GM suspesion was the SS version of the S-10 pickup that was supposed to achieve some phenomonal,high G rating.After driving for a few minutes,I looked underneath,and saw that the suspension was only 3/8 of an inch off of the urethane bumpstops.||||reg||1
